 """Optional throughput-oriented admission boundary for the native HTTP engine.
 
 Already admitted requests keep their normal scheduler and state ownership.
-After the first decode step, new HTTP requests wait for that finite cohort to
-finish. No timer, benchmark concurrency, prompt identity or response is used.
+Before freezing the first decoding cohort, give already queued requests an
+admission pass while HTTP capacity remains. Once frozen, new HTTP requests wait
+for that finite cohort to finish. No timer, benchmark concurrency, prompt
+identity or response is used.
 This trades admission latency for fewer mid-decode prefill interruptions; NPU
 performance and output validity require separate validation.
 """
